{"archetypes":[{"name":"pin-drift","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"Plan specifies multiple byte-exact grep literals that CI pins must match verbatim; a paraphrase or apostrophe error between the prose and the pin string silently breaks the harness while the feature appears shipped.","prompt_body":"Verify every grep literal the plan names for test scripts is a strict byte-identical substring of the prose the plan says will be written in AGENTS.md and orchestrator-never.md — not a paraphrase. The plan states the AGENTS.md bullet must contain `poll the task output file once per turn` (apostrophe-free) and the orchestrator-never.md rule must open with `NEVER poll a background task by reading its output file once per turn`; cross-check both literals against the verbatim text blocks in the plan. Confirm the test-design-structure.sh assertion uses the exact orchestrator-never.md opening sentence and that the test-implement-anti-polling-rule.sh `check` call uses the exact AGENTS.md substring. Flag any case where a pin literal is a paraphrase of the prose, contains a character the prose omits, or is taken from a different sentence than the one the plan points to. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"hook-gate-composition","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The hook gains three interacting changes — gate removal, case-branch split, and a new separate state file — that must compose without regressing existing Read coverage or letting the Bash branch silently discard events.","prompt_body":"Examine the plan's hook changes in `scripts/hook-anti-read-poll.sh` and `scripts/test-hook-anti-read-poll.sh` for composition hazards. Confirm the plan explicitly removes the Read-only `tool_name` guard (line 14) before the new `case` statement rather than relocating it inside a branch where it would still discard Bash events. Verify the plan's separate `state-taskout-<cwd_hash>.tsv` file is keyed by path only and cannot share keys with the generic state file so task-output counting and normal-path counting remain independent. Check whether the plan specifies initialization and cleanup semantics for the new state file, or leaves state accumulation unbounded. Confirm the Bash suffix-tolerant classifier (`tasks/[A-Za-z0-9._-]+\\.output` without end-anchoring the full command) and the Read end-anchored classifier are kept in separate branches so a Read event against a task-output path is not double-counted via the Bash branch. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
